A.1.0. {"domain": "authoring", "check": "capability", "severity": "info", "where": "actions.skip_stage", "problem": "Draft.open via skip_stage from open is narrower", "carried": false, "from": "compiler"}
A.1.1. {"problem": "The new precondition `reason-written` (`exists(params.reason)`) cannot deny anything. `reason` is a required, non-optional string param, so it always exists, and an empty string passes. The rule 'a stage is skipped only with the owner's written reason' is therefore not enforced, and the change request's condition ('if they write why') is not met. The check should test for non-empty text, or the param should be validated.", "where": "authoring.domain.yaml, action skip_stage, precondition reason-written", "kind": "other", "from": "llm"}
A.1.2. {"problem": "The diff sets skip_stage to `status: proposed`, but the file after the change shows `status: confirmed`, with a source of `interview:domains/authoring/interview.jsonl#L47` and no quote. The element loosens a gate and no person has confirmed it, which contradicts the domain's own rule that elements are confirmed only by a person. Either the status is wrong in the file, or a proposed element is being deployed as if confirmed. The new interview ref is not backed by a quote, and the change request's 'Why:' is empty.", "where": "authoring.domain.yaml, action skip_stage, status and source", "kind": "contradiction", "from": "llm"}
A.1.3. {"problem": "The action's behaviour changed so that required stages can now be skipped, but the domain version (authoring 22) and the interface the composition pins (interface 1) were not bumped. The kernel `skip_stage` call that the effect makes may still refuse required stages, because it is outside this declaration and nothing in the diff changes it. If it does, the new description promises something the deployed system does not do. The ADR-0025 staged-interview source for Draft also treats required stages as required, and nothing reconciles it with the change.", "where": "authoring.domain.yaml, version and skip_stage effect call; toprope-self.composition.yaml, authoring interface 1", "kind": "behaviour", "from": "llm"}
A.1.4. {"problem": "The written reason is never stored in the domain. `record_skip` takes only `skipped` and sets nothing, and Draft has no property for the reason. A skipped required stage leaves no visible justification, and no scenario covers skip_stage with a required stage or a missing reason.", "where": "authoring.domain.yaml, record_skip, Draft object, scenarios", "kind": "other", "from": "llm"}
A.2.0. {"domain": "authoring", "check": "capability", "severity": "info", "where": "actions.skip_stage", "problem": "Draft.open via skip_stage from open is narrower", "carried": false, "from": "compiler"}
A.2.1. {"problem": "The new precondition `exists(params.reason)` checks nothing. `reason` is already a required string param on skip_stage, so it always exists, and an empty or whitespace-only string would still pass. The rule 'skip only with a written why' is therefore not enforced.", "where": "authoring.domain.yaml, action skip_stage, precondition reason-written", "kind": "other", "from": "llm"}
A.2.2. {"problem": "The domain has no notion of required versus optional stages. Stage handling lives in the kernel's `skip_stage` call and the staged interview (ADR-0025). The declaration change only rewrites the description and adds a vacuous precondition, so a required stage may still be refused by the kernel. The stated behaviour change may never take effect, and nothing in the domain or in a scenario shows it does.", "where": "authoring.domain.yaml, action skip_stage (effects call skip_stage)", "kind": "behaviour", "from": "llm"}
A.2.3. {"problem": "The diff sets skip_stage to `status: proposed`, but the file after the change shows `status: confirmed`. The new behaviour is cited to an interview line, and confirmation needs a person (confirm_element requires human). The element looks self-confirmed, or the diff and file disagree. The new source `interview:...#L47` has no quote, and the change request's 'Why' is blank, so nothing supports that line. It is also later than any line cited elsewhere in the file (L42 is the latest).", "where": "authoring.domain.yaml, skip_stage source/status", "kind": "other", "from": "llm"}
A.2.4. {"problem": "The change loosens a safeguard: a required interview stage can now be skipped. The old description and the ADR-0037 source said only an optional stage could be skipped. The Draft transition (skip_stage and record_skip) and the other record-based sources still rest on the old behaviour. The new rule is not carried into the glossary (draft, element) or into the Draft matrix source.", "where": "authoring.domain.yaml, transitions.Draft.skip_stage / glossary", "kind": "reference", "from": "llm"}
A.2.5. {"problem": "No scenario covers the new precondition `reason-written` or skipping a required stage. A denial or an allowed skip would go untested, and no fixture exists for a required stage.", "where": "authoring.domain.yaml, scenarios / world", "kind": "other", "from": "llm"}
