A.5.2. {"problem": "The diff and the file after the change disagree about the status of skip_stage. The diff sets `status: proposed`, but the file as it stands shows `status: confirmed`, with a new interview source (interview.jsonl#L47) that has no quote. A behaviour change that lets owners bypass required stages should not be marked confirmed unless a person confirmed it. The cited interview line cannot be checked here, and no other element cites a line beyond L42.", "where": "authoring.domain.yaml, action skip_stage, source and status", "kind": "other", "from": "llm"}
A.5.3. {"problem": "The reason is not kept anywhere. `record_skip` takes only `skipped: boolean`, and Draft has no field for it. Skipping a required stage is now allowed 'if the owner writes why', so there is no record of that reason in the declared state. It can only be passed to the kernel call.", "where": "authoring.domain.yaml, record_skip and object Draft", "kind": "behaviour", "from": "llm"}
